.TH "WEBGLACTIVEINFO" "3JS" "October 6, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebGLActiveInfo \- WebGLActiveInfo
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]WebGLActiveInfo\f[B]\f[R] interface is part of the WebGL
API and represents the information returned by calling the
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getActiveAttrib()\f[R] and
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getActiveUniform()\f[R] methods.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]WebGLActiveInfo.name\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
The name of the requested variable.
.TP
\f[B]WebGLActiveInfo.size\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
The size of the requested variable.
.TP
\f[B]WebGLActiveInfo.type\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
The type of the requested variable.
.SH EXAMPLES
A \f[CR]WebGLActiveInfo\f[R] object is returned by:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getActiveAttrib()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getActiveUniform()\f[R] or
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGL2RenderingContext.getTransformFeedbackVarying()\f[R]
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getActiveAttrib()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext.getActiveUniform()\f[R]
